Terraform Output Variables
What are Output Variables?
Output variables expose information about your infrastructure on the command line and 
can share data between Terraform modules. 
They are useful for:
Displaying important resource attributes after apply
Passing data between modules
Providing information for external scripts or automation
Best Practices
Always add descriptions to outputs for documentation
Mark sensitive outputs appropriately
Use meaningful names that describe the value
Group related outputs together
Use outputs for module interfaces to expose necessary data
