Terraform Resource Attributes
What are Resource Attributes?
Resource attributes are the properties of infrastructure resources that Terraform manages. There are two types:

Arguments: Values you set to configure the resource ( like a instance id creation)
Attributes: Values that are computed/returned by the provider after resource creation
( getting auto created like public ip ,You reference them, not set them)

Best Practices
Use attributes for dependencies instead of hardcoding values
Reference computed attributes in outputs for visibility
Use splat expressions for resources with count
Use for expressions for resources with for_each
Check documentation for all available attributes
------------------------
What are Resource Dependencies?
Resource dependencies define the order in which Terraform creates, updates, or destroys resources. Terraform uses dependencies to build a dependency graph and determine the correct order of operations.

Types of Dependencies
Implicit Dependencies: Automatically created when you reference resource attributes
  vpc_id     = aws_vpc.main.id    # <-- This creates an implicit dependenc
Explicit Dependencies: Manually specified using depends_on
Use depends_on when there's a dependency that Terraform can't automatically detect.
Dependency Order
Creation Order
Resources are created from leaves to root of the dependency tree:

Resources with no dependencies first
Then resources that depend on those
Continue until all resources are created
Destruction Order
Resources are destroyed in reverse order:

Resources that nothing depends on first
Then their dependencies
Continue until all resources are destroyed
